            <ArticleTitle>Spasm of the left main coronary artery: an indication for surgery?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>239-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with severe angina at rest was studied by coronary angiography. A severe spasm in the left main coronary artery was observed; after nifedipine and isosorbide dinitrate a moderate stenosis was still present and surgery was successfully performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
